// Rich text editor — proposed schema changes
//
// PROPOSAL ONLY. Nothing here has been applied. `prisma/schema.prisma` was
// off-limits for this task, so this file records the exact edits the owner of
// that file should make.
//
// Companion: .plan/editor-deps.md
//
// Shape of the change: two nullable Json columns. Nothing is dropped, nothing
// is renamed, nothing changes type. Additive only, so it is safe to apply
// ahead of any code and safe to leave applied if the code is rolled back.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHY Json AND NOT A `descriptionFormat` DISCRIMINATOR
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Nullness is the discriminator, so no extra column is needed:
//
//   descriptionJson IS NULL      -> legacy row, `description` is plain text,
//                                   render it escaped with newlines preserved
//   descriptionJson IS NOT NULL  -> rich row, render the doc through the
//                                   allowlist walker; `description` is now a
//                                   server-derived plaintext MIRROR of the doc
//
// The existing String columns keep their meaning for every consumer that reads
// them today (JQL `~`, search, notification excerpts, Slack/Teams payloads,
// automation): they are always plain text, before and after. That is the whole
// back-compat story and it needs no backfill.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// COCKROACHDB NOTE
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Prisma maps `Json` to JSONB on both PostgreSQL and CockroachDB. Adding a
// nullable JSONB column is a metadata-only change on both — no table rewrite,
// no lock held over the data. Safe to `prisma db push` against a live DB.
//
// Do NOT add a GIN index on these columns. Nothing queries inside the document;
// all searching goes through the plaintext mirror. A GIN index on JSONB would
// cost write throughput for zero read benefit.


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 1. model Issue — add ONE line
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// In prisma/schema.prisma, immediately after the existing
//     description      String?
// line (currently line 242), add:

  descriptionJson  Json?          // ProseMirror/TipTap doc. NULL => `description` is legacy plain text.
                                  // When set, `description` is the derived plaintext mirror.


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 2. model Comment — add ONE line
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// In prisma/schema.prisma, immediately after the existing
//     body      String
// line (currently line 290), add:

  bodyJson  Json?    // ProseMirror/TipTap doc. NULL => `body` is legacy plain text.
                     // When set, `body` is the derived plaintext mirror.


