// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// SELECT/INCLUDE SITES THAT MUST BE UPDATED
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Anywhere that uses an explicit `select` rather than a full-row fetch has to
// opt the new columns in, or the UI silently stays in legacy plaintext mode.
// Grep before applying:
//
//   grep -rn "description: true" lib/ app/
//   grep -rn "body: true"        lib/ app/
//
// `getIssueByKey` in lib/issues.ts is the one that feeds the issue detail page.


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// DELIBERATELY NOT INCLUDED
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The repo's own V2-3a spec
// (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-21-trackly-v2-3a-editor-comments-worklog-design.md)
// also proposes CommentMention, CommentReaction, CommentEdit, Worklog and
// Site.hoursPerDay. Those belong to comments-v2 and time-tracking, not to the
// editor, and none of them is needed for rich text to work. They are omitted
// here on purpose so this proposal stays reviewable as one change.
//
// One connection worth flagging: once `bodyJson` exists,
// `extractMentionUserIds(bodyJson)` (components/editor/text.ts) gives exact
// user ids at write time, which is what a future CommentMention table would
// store. Until that table exists, mentions still notify via the existing
// name-regex path reading the plaintext mirror — see .plan/editor-deps.md,
// "Server-side wiring still required".


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// APPLYING
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   npm run db:push       # additive, no data loss
//   npx prisma generate   # runs automatically via postinstall/build
//
// No `prisma migrate` step is needed for a dev database. For production, an
// `ADD COLUMN ... JSONB NULL` migration is the equivalent and is non-blocking.
